&#8220;He&#8217;s probably sold more stuff than me,&#8221; Pillsbury said of King, who indeed is one of the best-selling novelists of all time. &#8220;Got more money.&#8221;

After a bit of back-and-forth, Dimoldenberg told the singer: &#8220;You&#8217;re not as successful as Stephen King, no. That&#8217;s just a fact.&#8221;

&#8220;You&#8217;re starting to hurt my feelings,&#8221; Pillsbury replied. &#8220;[He has a] whole different job.&#8221;

The jury&#8217;s still out on who exactly is Maine&#8217;s most famous celebrity, but other front-runners include actor Patrick Dempsey and sports personality Erin Andrews. And while Role Model may not quite have the sales numbers that King has, the musician recently scored his very first top 10 album on the Billboard 200 with Chuck Timely & The Hourglass , which amassed 24,000 copies sold in the United States in its first week out, according to Luminate.

The new album also features a collaboration with Pillsbury&#8217;s then-girlfriend Dakota Johnson, who contributes a spoken-word section to &#8220;Love I You.&#8221; And, speaking of the brunette actress&#8230;

Later in their conversation, Dimoldenberg asked the star what his &#8220;type&#8221; is, to which he initially told the blonde British personality, &#8220;You&#8217;re not gonna like it, so I&#8217;m going to lie. I&#8217;m going to say I just love people.&#8221;

After Dimoldenberg got him to admit that he prefers brunettes, Pillsbury joked, &#8220;I think some people can be brunette on the inside. I feel a real connection to you in a brunette sort of way.&#8221;

